SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri\, Adamas
LOCATION:Adamas\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The port's Dekapentavgoustos: vespers and bread-blessing at 20:00 on 14 August followed by a procession of the icon around the harbour\, liturgy at 07:30 on the 15th\, and from 21:30 on the 15th a traditional glenti with violins and laouto in the church courtyard. It is the busiest night of the year in Adamas — book dinner and accommodation well ahead\, and expect the harbour road to be closed for the procession.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#adamas-dormition-panigiri-adamas
